## Changes

**Comment & Template microservices:**
- Removed `SeedData()` methods from DbContext classes
- Implemented `UseSeeding` in Program.cs with environment guard
- Added `UseAsyncSeeding` for automatic migration application in Development
- Regenerated migrations (Comment: 103→76 lines, Template: 312→257 lines)

**Template microservice only:**
- Added `TemplateDbContextFactory` for EF Core design-time operations

## Pattern

```csharp
builder.Services.AddDbContext<CommentDbContext>(options =>
    options.UseSqlServer(connectionString)
           .UseSeeding((context, _) =>
           {
               if (builder.Environment.IsDevelopment()) 
               {
                   if (!context.Set<Template>().Any())
                   {
                       context.Set<Template>().AddRange(templates);
                       context.SaveChanges();
                   }
               }
           })
           .UseAsyncSeeding(async (context, _, cancellationToken) =>
           {
               if (builder.Environment.IsDevelopment())
                   await context.Database.MigrateAsync(cancellationToken);
           }));
```

## Impact

- Migrations contain only schema definitions
- Seed data idempotent (checks existence before insert)
- Development: auto-migrates + seeds; Production: clean slate
- Tests: 128/128 passing

