## Problem

Three issues: setup wizard gated behind config (blocking first-time admin setup), `/setup-lobby` command registered in Discord but no handler (causing "application did not respond" errors), and voice channel control panels not appearing in chat.

## Changes

### Command Registration Sync

- Added `/setup-lobby` to `loadCommandsDynamically()` - was only in `populateClientCommands()`, causing handler/registration mismatch
- Changed `/setup` from `configKey: "wizard.enabled"` to `configKey: null` - setup wizard now always available as core feature

**In `src/services/command-manager.ts`:**
```typescript
// Before: only in populateClientCommands()
{ name: "setup-lobby", configKey: null, file: "setup-lobby" }

// Before: gated by config
{ name: "setup", configKey: "wizard.enabled", file: "setup-wizard" }

// After: in both arrays, setup always enabled
{ name: "setup", configKey: null, file: "setup-wizard" },
{ name: "setup-lobby", configKey: null, file: "setup-lobby" },
```

### Voice Channel Control Panel

- Check for `send` method existence before attempting to message voice channels (not all voice channels support direct messaging)
- Fallback to finding text channel with same name in category if voice channel messaging unavailable
- Added debug logging for troubleshooting send failures

**In `src/services/voice-channel-manager.ts`:**
```typescript
// Check capability before attempting
if ("send" in channel && typeof channel.send === "function") {
  try {
    await channel.send({ content, embeds, components });
    return;
  } catch (error) {
    logger.debug(`Failed to send to voice channel, trying fallback`, error);
  }
}

// Fallback to text channel in same category
const textChannel = category.children.cache.find(
  (ch) => ch.type === ChannelType.GuildText && ch.name === channel.name
) as TextChannel | undefined;
```

### Tests

- Added validation that command arrays stay synchronized between registration methods
- Added validation that setup command remains always-enabled

